WEBVTT

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.940
It's time to settle things, partner.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:02:01.030
Traces of Crime

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:11.190
It smells good, but...
I'll just stick with milk.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:17.860
So, he really did run away
from the EMS interrogation.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:21.320
Yeah, well, that's fine.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.570
Sorry, but can you leave this to me?

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:28.570
I owe you one, Olivier.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.940
Where is Mary?

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:38.650
I haven't seen her today. Lefty, too.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.730
Oh. She's at the doctor.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:45.480
She doesn't know how to
fix flesh wounds, after all.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.650
By the way, that voice of yours...

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:51.230
Spitzbergen did the procedure.

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:54.690
They must have really wanted
to talk with me directly.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.360
It surprised me.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:02.030
They hate extension technology,
but they have engineers as good as Mary.

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:06.780
Now I don't have to carry around
the head of an Extended, anymore.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.280
I see.

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.440
Oh, about Chris.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:19.730
She was in a pretty weak state, so they're
hospitalizing her for two or three days.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:22.150
But it seems like she's
doing great otherwise.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:26.150
I see. That's good.

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:30.900
Juzo, what are you doing?!

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.440
Well, you know.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:41.110
My actions put you guys in danger.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.860
Sorry about that.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:50.820
I have no idea what happened to you guys,
but you saved Chris, didn't you?

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:54.400
You did what I had to do in my place.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:58.650
Thanks, Tetsuro.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:04.280
Juzo, I...

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:08.480
Um, excuse me...

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:11.360
Am I at the right place?

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.030
I am looking for Mr. Inui's consulting office...

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:19.570
My name is Emma Kurtz.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.230
Sorry.

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:24.780
It's breezy because of a small
problem we had with the wall.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:29.480
No, the coffee is keeping me warm.

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.650
Even so...

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:34.980
You aren't surprised seeing my face?

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.730
Oh, yes.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:39.650
It's surprising, of course.

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:45.610
But I had heard the rumors and
I'm close to someone similar to you.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:52.150
Does it bother you?

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:55.570
I'm actually quite the tomboy
and have a lot of scars.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:58.320
Oh, no, that's not...

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:01.940
So, what business do you have with me?

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:07.530
Yes. I'd like you to find my husband, Edmund.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:14.070
In truth, while this isn't
uncommon in this day and age,

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:18.320
I lost my fiancé during the great war.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:23.570
I had loved my fiancé, Theodore, dearly.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.070
We weren't together very long.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:31.860
Even so, the time I spent with him
brought me great happiness.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:42.730
But when I received news of his death,
my grief made me attempt suicide.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:53.650
The one who saved me...
is my current husband, Edmund.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:56.480
He looks like you.

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:58.440
He doesn't!

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:04.360
Ed was severely injured and most of his
body was replaced with extensions.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:10.440
He happened to be in the same
unit as my fiancé, Theodore.

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:16.400
They were both part of the
bomb disposal unit after the war,

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.530
but there was an accident...

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:20.980
They were both caught in an explosion.

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:29.150
My fiancé, Theodore, died,
but Ed managed to survive.

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:34.030
When I heard about their relationship,

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:42.440
I felt like Theodore had sent
Edmund to save me from myself.

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:46.980
I may sound like a cold-hearted woman,

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:50.320
but I was past the age of naïvety.

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:52.900
Once we confirmed our
feelings for one another,

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:57.610
it did not take long for us to marry.

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:01.780
What is it, Juzo? The bathroom?

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:07.530
No. These types of stories just
make me a bit uncomfortable.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:13.440
A month ago, I noticed that
Ed was acting strange.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:18.570
He would be gone for days
without a single word.

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:23.570
Then, three days ago...

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:30.110
...my husband came home
with a new arm extension.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:37.150
He kissed me gently on
the forehead and told me,

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:42.190
"Emma, there's something I gotta do.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:47.190
I promise I'll come back to you once I'm done."

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.030
Over extensions...

00:07:54.030 --> 00:08:02.230
In other words, your husband may have
a reason to hurt someone somewhere.

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:05.650
You think so, too. As I thought.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:13.320
Mr. Inui, do the habits an Extended had
while still flesh and blood usually remain?

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:14.530
Who knows?

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:18.440
Unfortunately, I don't have any memories
from when I was flesh and blood.

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:20.280
What about it?

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:26.360
The only body of an Extended
that I've touched is my husband's,

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:31.900
but I feel nostalgia when he holds me.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:33.610
What are you doing?!

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.730
Mr. Inui, please!

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:43.360
Please bring my husband, Ed,
back to me before it's too late!

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:50.110
Is it all right for me to come?

00:08:50.110 --> 00:08:52.650
It can't be helped.

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:59.070
The EMS stopped guarding us and
I can't just leave you alone here.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:14.530
We would like you to use Harmony to
pull out his true form, Master Tetsuro.

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:20.320
What's wrong?

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:23.280
I don't plan on babysitting a kid.

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:25.570
Y-Yeah. I know!

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:34.070
But Juzo. Do you have an idea
on Edmund's whereabouts?

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:40.780
Nope. That's why we're
going to look into him first.

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:44.860
Please use the third window for any
issues regarding bereavement pay.

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:48.020
"Roster Division Reception Counter"
"Meeting Room 3"

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:50.530
Please use the fifth window for
questions regarding work rehabilitation.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:52.730
What? You can't show me the register?

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:56.530
Please use the seventh window for
questions on extension technology.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:10:02.730
Front Desk (Large)

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.780
I'm not talking about the register!

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.730
The person you're looking for. Um...

00:09:57.730 --> 00:10:02.730
Edmund Baker is a restricted record.

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:06.110
I didn't know there were records like this.

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:09.480
By the way, you're an
Over-Extended, aren't you?

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.150
I have my license if you need it.

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:13.730
That means that you're a military veteran.

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:15.570
How strange...

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:19.980
I have a lot of confidence in my memory.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:24.320
Yet, I've never seen you
on the military register!

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:27.280
Sorry, I should have showed
you my paperwork sooner.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:31.280
Oh, my.

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:33.610
You really do have exemption.

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:35.530
What in the world?

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:39.650
My memory is never wrong...

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:41.230
Sorry for the trouble.

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:42.360
Oh, wait.

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:42.360
Juzo?

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:47.400
About the support fund for
helping disabled war veterans...!

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:47.400
Juzo, are you stopping?

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:51.110
Yeah. We got something out of it.

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:55.480
We found out that she didn't know about Edmund.

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.860
How is that useful?

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:02.730
That civil servant said she's never
seen me on the register, right?

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:08.940
That's because my records are restricted,
just like Edmund's.

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:10.690
That means...

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:14.860
We're both people that the
higher-ups want to hide.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:22.360
In other words, Edmund and I
are birds of a feather.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.730
He's like you, Juzo?

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:35.360
Don't worry.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:38.610
It doesn't hurt anymore as
long as I don't push myself.

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:43.320
More importantly,
I'm completely broke this month.

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:48.190
I wish there was a rich customer
lying around nearby...

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:52.070
I know.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:56.570
There's no way I'd be that lucky...

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:57.780
Huh?

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.070
Oh?

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:08.190
We looked for so long and
we couldn't find a single clue.

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:10.860
Guess we'll have to
check the sedative routes...

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:15.110
Or, I don't want to, but I can ask
some retired veterans I know.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:20.820
Where the hell did you go, Mr. Edmund?

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:22.980
Amazing!

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:25.900
Colt?!

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:32.360
I'm so moved to find such a
young extension engineer!

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:34.860
I-I got it. Please let go!

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:34.860
Doc, you're amazing!

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:37.030
Oh! My bad. My bad.

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:38.150
Goodness.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:41.860
Why did you use a month's worth
of sedatives all at once?!

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:43.360
There are limits, you know!

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:47.530
Well... I'm the type that likes to go wild!

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:49.820
"Love"

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:49.820
I was trying to get myself pumped up.

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:52.360
I'm surprised you're still alive.

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:53.980
Don't fall for me, Doc.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:56.650
Where'd you get that idea?!

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:59.400
Oh, Juzo.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:01.280
Why are you here?

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:02.190
Huh?

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:06.070
Well, well. What an utterly
unexpected turn of events!

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:09.030
I found him lying on the side of the road.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:11.530
I couldn't just leave him there,
so I brought him here to patch him up.

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:15.480
I can't destroy the house of
someone who saved my life.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:17.980
No, this isn't my house--

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:20.150
Wait, destroy?

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:21.780
Come with me.

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:24.900
You got business with me, right?

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:26.400
Thanks for the help, Doc!

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:29.030
I'll definitely return the favor someday!

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:32.780
S-Someone you know?

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:40.480
A ghost?

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:45.230
Yeah, that's why that basement is off limits.

00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:47.070
Let's go check it out.

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:48.480
But...

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:50.650
Hey, kids.

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:53.610
Take this and go get some candy for yourselves.

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:55.440
Seriously?

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:56.280
Whoa!

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:57.570
All right!

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:58.940
Thanks, old man.

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:01.150
Yeah. Hurry up and go.

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:02.730
Okay!

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.570
Don't come over this way for a while.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:08.480
Kids are so quick to adapt.

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:12.730
They don't even get surprised when they see us.

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:16.190
Edmund Baker, right?

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:19.610
You're pretty different from
how she described you.

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:23.150
She made you seem like
a prince on a white horse.

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:24.780
Emma, was it?

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:30.900
Your other half was pretty worried about you.

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:32.360
That so.

00:14:32.360 --> 00:14:37.110
My suspicions were right on the mark.

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:41.280
Then, let's hurry up and end this!

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.530
What the hell?! So suddenly!

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:52.730
Stop! What the hell are you doing?!

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:01.530
Now I've got you.

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:06.690
This guy. His movements are wild,
but he's experienced at fighting.

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:16.110
Bastard... Don't lay your hands on my Emma!

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:19.820
Huh? I think you've got the wrong idea?

00:15:19.820 --> 00:15:21.190
Don't play dumb!

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:25.190
You messed with the wrong guy, partner!

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:28.440
Partner...?

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:32.030
Juzo is late.

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:37.150
Juzo said he and Edmund
were two birds of a feather...

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:39.610
Huh? You mean...?

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:42.820
Speak of the devil.

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:43.940
Miss Emma!

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:45.860
A client?

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:48.650
Perfect timing! We found your husband.

00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:49.940
He's with Juzo1

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:52.980
That's what I thought.

00:15:52.980 --> 00:15:55.150
Huh?

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:58.110
I'm sorry. Please forgive me!

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.480
How many years has it been now?

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:07.230
I really thought I had gotten away.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:13.070
But I was wrong. That day...

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:18.980
After seeing that attack
that destroyed everything...

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:21.570
I was chilled to the bone.

00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:26.730
That was a message from you.

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:29.570
Even if I change my name or my form,

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:32.940
you'd find me to get revenge.

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:34.320
No. Hey, that's...

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:38.650
But I can't let myself die by your hands!

00:16:38.650 --> 00:16:41.280
That's why I got myself good and ready!

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:43.860
I'm gonna finish you off with my own hands!

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:45.030
Listen to me!

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:47.730
Enough talk!

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:49.820
Don't just say what you want!

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:51.730
You're so hard-headed!

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:57.440
You Gun Slave Units are covered
in an skin of insulation.

00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:59.530
Gun Slave Unit?!

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:02.360
Just like I thought!

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:09.320
But the special electric needles I just
punched into you can bypass that!

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:10.530
What?!

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:16.230
Now, let's test it out with a bang!

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:20.150
I wonder what'll happen to that
head filled with gunpowder...

00:17:20.150 --> 00:17:22.650
...with a crazy burst electricity!

00:17:24.860 --> 00:17:26.070
Juzo!

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:29.570
Here's some candy.

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:31.070
Split with that old man.

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:33.230
One of the kids!

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:37.780
Lightning and Thunder! Unstoppable Strike!

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:47.820
Over there!

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:09.030
I told you not to come back for a while.

00:18:09.030 --> 00:18:10.230
Go on.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:12.440
Okay... See ya.

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:16.860
Why?

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:19.980
Why didn't you strike me down?

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:22.400
I'd like to ask you, too.

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:26.860
Why'd you throw that kid my way?

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:29.360
Thought you'd protect yourself
with insulation extensions

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:33.480
if you planned to use that kind of attack.

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:41.730
I see. You protected an unrelated
kid before protecting yourself.

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:45.860
You aren't my partner, Five, are you?

00:18:45.860 --> 00:18:47.480
I told you already!

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:50.690
You should confirm things
before trying to kill a person!

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:52.440
My bad. My bad.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:56.730
I mean, frankly, all of you
guys look exactly alike.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:59.230
Juzo! Are you all right?!

00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:00.190
Tetsuro...

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:01.150
Emma?

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:04.070
What's wrong with you two?

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:09.030
This person knew that Edmund was
looking for you when she asked for you.

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:13.230
She wanted you to appear before Edmund.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:15.030
I see.

00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:18.900
So, you came looking for me
in your husband's place.

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:23.690
Why, Emma? Why'd you do such a thing?

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:26.070
I'm sorry.

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:28.190
After you went missing...

00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:31.070
...I realized you were looking for a man
with a gun for a head as soon as I looked

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:34.940
through the pictures and
news articles you left behind.

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:38.940
Come to think of it, I left
everything all over the place.

00:19:40.230 --> 00:19:46.440
Considering your wild personality,
I had no idea when you'd finish.

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:50.030
I didn't know when you'd come home...

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:53.940
I don't want to be alone anymore.

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:58.070
I'm sorry.

00:19:58.070 --> 00:20:03.030
Ed... you're Theodore, aren't you?

00:20:03.030 --> 00:20:05.400
Wh-What are you talking about, Emma?

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:06.730
I'm...

00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:12.150
You always kiss my scar
when you make love to me.

00:20:12.150 --> 00:20:13.570
Why?

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:19.110
Hey! Don't say such embarrassing
things in front of other people!

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.480
I-I don't do anything like that!

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:22.690
Like that?

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:27.320
N-No, it's just that you
always worry about that scar.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:30.940
I wanted to show you I love you
along with that scar of yours...

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:34.400
Theodore told me the exact same thing.

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:39.690
That's the reason I no longer try
to hide this scar from others.

00:20:39.690 --> 00:20:41.070
Haven't you noticed?

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:47.190
I've never worried about
my scar around <i>you</i> before.

00:20:47.190 --> 00:20:48.570
Ed.

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:55.440
I can't win against you, Emma.

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:58.900
I'm sorry for deceiving you.

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:02.690
It's okay. I was never deceived.

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:04.110
Don't praise me like that!

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:06.030
I wasn't praising you, silly.

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:07.570
What the hell is this?

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:11.650
But why did you have to pretend
like you were someone else?

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:12.980
That's...

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:20.320
You created a fake identity to keep
your partner, Five, from finding you.

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:27.150
You didn't want Five to get revenge
on you and the people around you.

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:28.360
Five?

00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:31.980
You know him?

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:35.650
I remember him well.

00:21:35.650 --> 00:21:37.530
Then, will you tell me?

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:39.820
Where is he now?!

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:42.440
Once I know that, I can...

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:48.360
There's no need.

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:54.610
I already took care of that guy
with my own hands six years ago.

00:23:27.610 --> 00:23:32.190
Juzo, you always fight for someone else.

00:23:28.480 --> 00:23:30.820
You're a Hands.

00:23:30.820 --> 00:23:35.480
Why did you eliminate my partner?

00:23:32.190 --> 00:23:35.480
Does Juzo regret it?

00:23:35.480 --> 00:23:41.940
<i>NO GUNS LIFE</i> . Episode 19.
"Scar."
